 "/athletes/9885"} "Magdalena Wunderlich"] ", a relatively unheralded competitor. Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10447"} "Maria Ćwiertniewicz"] ", meanwhile, was a distant third. Bahmann underwent a massive improvement in the second run and posted an impressive score that was more than sufficient to win gold. The biggest jump, however, came from West Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9866"} "Gisela Grothaus"] ", who was ninth in round one, but runner-up in the second round and earned enough points to nab the silver medal. Ćwiertniewicz, meanwhile, improved her score, but not enough to pass Wunderlich, whose run one score allowed her to take bronze."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Total Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "126"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9794"} "Angelika Bahmann"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "364.50"] [:td {} "413.07 (2)"] [:td {} "364.50 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "170"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9866"} "Gisela Grothaus"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRG.png"}] "FRG"]] [:td {} "398.15"] [:td {} "521.10 (9)"] [:td {} "398.15 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "193"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9885"} "Magdalena Wunderlich"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.e